  "description": "The colored Lawrence-Rozansky modulus identification on Sigma(2,3,5) -- the W_lambda keystone's last open piece. VERDICT: CORRECTED EXACT IDENTITY. The color-alpha insertion on the order-5 fibre produces the Hikami odd character chi^(1,1,alpha); computed exactly, the map alpha -> chi factors through the r=5 affine-Weyl fold with the SAME kernel and signs as alpha -> [alpha]_zeta at the fibre root zeta = e^{i pi/5} (chi^(114)=+chi^(111) ~ [4]=+[1]; chi^(113)=+chi^(112) ~ [3]=+[2]; chi^(115)=0 ~ [5]=0; chi^(116)=-chi^(111) ~ [6]=-[1]). The colored Gauss sum tau_N(alpha) (alpha=1 anchors to bare Theorem 10 machine-zero) obeys the fold AT THE FLAT-CONNECTION LEVEL: the class deviations are ELEMENTARY exact identities -- tau_N(4)-tau_N(1) = 1+2cos(2pi/N) and tau_N(3)-tau_N(2) = e^{-6pi i/(5N)} (machine zero at N=7,11,13,25), tau_N(6)+tau_N(1) bounded after Cor-12 normalization, tau_N(5) has NO flat part. Flat-connection amplitudes extracted parameter-free match A_m(alpha) = (2/sqrt5)sin(alpha m pi/5), and the EXACT Q(sqrt5) algebra gives, for every affine-E8 McKay node lambda (marks 1,2,3,4,5,6,4,2,3 = 2I irrep dims) and both flat connections m: |A_m(mark)| * D_E8(zeta^m) = 2*|[mark]_{zeta^m}| with D_E8(zeta^m)^2 = 10 +- 2sqrt5 and core identity (10-2sqrt5)(10+2sqrt5)=80. So |S_0lambda^(m)| = 2*d_{zeta^m}(lambda)/D_E8 = sqrt2*d/D_MTC (D_E8^2 = 2*D_MTC^2, the 2:1 fold of the affine-E8 node set onto the r=5 alcove). Corrections to the conjectured shape: (1) zeta is the FIBRE root e^{m pi i/5} Galois-indexed by the flat connection, not the level root and not e^{2 pi i/30}; (2) global factor 2 (resp. sqrt2); (3) the identity lives at the FOLDED D=2 level -- the 4 generic-q Hecke classes collapse at the fibre root ((3,2) muon class -> [5]=0; electron [5]+1 = 1 = |[6]|, moduli consistent); the 9-independent-moduli reading at a single zeta is (b)-excluded by D(2,3,5)=2 (two irreducible SU(2) flat connections, Fintushel-Stern; machine-validated in-repo). The generic-q/archimedean separation remains the standing open continuation (#3652/#3681). No fit; nothing wired to production.",
